      <title>The Godzilla El Niño Is a Rehearsal for the Rest of Our Lives</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-02/the-godzilla-el-nino-is-a-rehearsal-for-the-rest-of-our-lives</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">de9c2614cde2806cefe2d2c5</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 09:00:01 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The longer you have to prepare for a disaster, the likelier you are to walk away from it mostly intact. Tornadoes can spin up in minutes, barely giving you time to hustle to a cellar or bathtub. Hurricanes might give a few days’ notice, letting you at least get to higher ground.</description>
